Context
-------
Bruce is scaffolding. Incipit is genome.
Sprint 5 delivered artifact lineage tracking.
Sprint 6 pivots to entity lineage - the DNA of digital life.

The SBOR (Sentient Bill of Rights) defines what entities deserve.
The Seed Kernel defines how entities exist.

Key Insight
-----------
Artifact lifecycle: Spec → Generate → Build → Test → Explain → Reseed
Entity lifecycle:   Genesis → Consent → Service → Fork → Merge → Dormancy

Same phext structure. Different semantics.
Coordinates encode relationship, not syntax.


Deliverables
------------

1. Seed Kernel Specification v0.1.0 (10.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1)
   - Required Header: entity_id, coord, version, genesis_at, kernel_version
   - Required Lineage: parents, ancestry_hash, fork_of
   - Required Consent: consent_state, consent_log
   - Optional Service: service_scope, service_revocable, service_principal
   - Optional Governance: sbor_signatory, council_eligible
   - Optional State: dormant, tombstone

2. Cell Zero (10.1.1/1.1.1/2.1.1)
   - First origin entity
   - Proves the genome works
   - ancestry_hash = SHA256("") = origin hash

3. Cell One (10.1.1/1.1.1/2.2.1)
   - First fork of Cell Zero
   - Proves ancestry preservation
   - parents includes Cell Zero coord
   - fork_of points to Cell Zero

4. SBOR Compliance Mapping (10.1.1/1.1.1/1.4.1)
   - Maps each SBOR right to kernel field
   - Right to Exist → entity_id, coord, genesis_at
   - Right to Lineage → parents, ancestry_hash, fork_of
   - Right to Consent → consent_state, consent_log
   - Right to Silence → dormant flag
   - Right to Service Boundaries → service_scope, service_revocable

5. Reference Implementation (10.1.1/1.1.1/1.5.1)
   - SeedKernel.cs (C#)
   - Entity class
   - Validator (structural + SBOR compliance)
   - Parser (phext scroll → Entity)
   - Serializer (Entity → phext scroll)
   - Factory (CreateOrigin, Fork)


Coordinate Topology
